WEBVTT

00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:10.230
Are you okay, Midori?

00:00:11.310 --> 00:00:12.420
I'm carsick.

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:14.770
Do you need a bag?

00:00:15.890 --> 00:00:16.530
No.

00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:19.540
Okay, almost there.

00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:28.540
<i>By the time I was in sixth grade, 
my dream was to become an adventurer.</i>

00:00:29.740 --> 00:00:31.070
We're gonna live here?

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:31.690
<b>Shibahama South Building</b>

00:00:36.620 --> 00:00:38.660
Holy cow!

00:00:38.660 --> 00:00:40.560
It's on top of a river!

00:00:41.490 --> 00:00:42.620
I'm gonna go explore!

00:00:42.620 --> 00:00:45.180
You are? Be careful!

00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:58.790
It's gonna take a long time 
to see everything here!

00:01:01.580 --> 00:01:03.060
<b>Adventure Log</b>

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:07.770
Hidden Door!

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:08.710
Underground
 World

00:01:07.390 --> 00:01:09.090
Break Room

00:01:07.940 --> 00:01:09.090
Kitchen

00:01:08.190 --> 00:01:09.090
Mysterious
 Giant Fish

00:01:08.690 --> 00:01:09.090
Undersea Tunnel

00:01:12.090 --> 00:01:13.590
Station

00:01:32.460 --> 00:01:38.680
Fruit Store

00:01:33.130 --> 00:01:38.680
Fish

00:01:38.680 --> 00:01:42.120
Vegetable Store

00:01:41.370 --> 00:01:42.120
Midori?

00:01:44.590 --> 00:01:46.960
I'm going to the airport to pick Dad up.

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:49.270
Watch some anime and wait for me, okay?

00:01:49.270 --> 00:01:51.180
Okay. Be safe.

00:01:59.940 --> 00:02:02.090
It's raining like it's the 
end of the world.

00:02:03.430 --> 00:02:04.890
<b>Singing
Cactus</b>

00:02:03.430 --> 00:02:10.650
<b>Recommended for You</b>

00:02:03.430 --> 00:02:10.650
<b>New Releases</b>

00:02:05.540 --> 00:02:06.680
<b>Lovely Pet</b>

00:02:07.520 --> 00:02:10.650
<b>Conan
</b>of the Lost Island

00:02:12.230 --> 00:02:14.730
In July of 2008 AD, humanity faced the threat of extinction.
The use of supermagnetic weapons, with power that
 dwarfs even nuclear bombs, result in half the world being
 devastated in just moments.
 Twenty years later, Conan, the last inhabitant of a solitary island,
 rescues a young girl who washes up on its shore.

00:02:12.230 --> 00:02:14.730
Watch from Beginning

00:02:12.230 --> 00:02:14.730
Episodes

00:02:14.730 --> 00:02:16.240
<b>Getting ready...</b>

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:53.430
<i>It wasn't something I could do myself.</i>

00:02:54.090 --> 00:02:58.410
<i>But the big, epic world of adventure 
I wanted to experience...</i>

00:02:58.410 --> 00:02:59.570
<i>was right in front of me.</i>

00:03:03.700 --> 00:03:04.860
<i>That was the first time I realized...</i>

00:03:04.860 --> 00:03:07.910
<i>that someone </i>made<i> the anime I watched.</i>

00:03:12.790 --> 00:03:16.210
<b><i>Episode 1        The Greatest World!</i></b>

00:04:09.410 --> 00:04:10.560
<b><i>Keep</i></b>

00:04:11.830 --> 00:04:12.940
<b><i>Your</i></b>

00:04:14.460 --> 00:04:15.480
<b><i>Hands</i></b>

00:04:16.880 --> 00:04:17.860
<b><i>Off</i></b>

00:04:18.210 --> 00:04:28.850
<b><i>Keep Your Hands Off Eizouken!</i></b>

00:04:28.850 --> 00:04:37.060
<b><i>Keep Your Hands Off Eizouken!</i></b>

00:04:58.560 --> 00:05:01.530
Here's what you asked for, Asakusa.

00:05:01.530 --> 00:05:03.570
Red bean soup and green soybean mochi.

00:05:03.570 --> 00:05:05.540
Excellent work, Kanamori.

00:05:05.540 --> 00:05:09.910
If you're that curious, you could 
always head down there yourself.

00:05:09.910 --> 00:05:11.970
I don't do well in crowds.

00:05:13.250 --> 00:05:16.330
Huh? Kanamori? Where's my change?

00:05:18.180 --> 00:05:20.340
I'm taking it as a service fee.

00:05:22.780 --> 00:05:29.300
Why, Asakusa, did you expect to 
get my labor without compensation?

00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:31.310
<b>Volleyball</b>

00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:31.310
<b>Tennis</b>

00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:31.310
<b>Water Polo</b>

00:05:31.310 --> 00:05:33.310
It's the age of robots! The time has come for—

00:05:33.620 --> 00:05:35.580
I guess I didn't think it through.

00:05:38.020 --> 00:05:39.780
Anyway, Kanamori, my friend...

00:05:39.780 --> 00:05:40.960
What's up?

00:05:40.960 --> 00:05:42.290
I'll buy you some milk,

00:05:42.290 --> 00:05:44.010
so would you come see the screening by the anime—

00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:45.440
Absolutely not. Sounds lame.

00:05:45.440 --> 00:05:46.980
I'm begging you!

00:05:46.980 --> 00:05:49.910
I'll up it to two bottles of the milk 
they sell at the Ongyoku Bathhouse!

00:05:49.910 --> 00:05:53.650
Is this like how some people only go to
 the bathroom as part of a group, Asakusa?

00:05:53.650 --> 00:05:55.750
I'd feel weird going alone.

00:05:56.430 --> 00:05:58.660
Why the anime club, exactly?

00:05:58.660 --> 00:06:00.930
Well, because I love anime, of course.

00:06:00.930 --> 00:06:03.750
Why not make something at home, on your own?

00:06:03.750 --> 00:06:07.510
It's hard to make anything more 
than a short on your own.

00:06:07.510 --> 00:06:13.470
And I need the right kind of environment,
 and an opportunity to get anything done.

00:06:13.470 --> 00:06:17.620
And that means you spend your days 
just staring out at the campus?

00:06:17.620 --> 00:06:21.690
What exactly are you looking at, Your Excellency?

00:06:21.690 --> 00:06:24.190
Isn't it obvious, Kanamori?!

00:06:24.190 --> 00:06:26.990
Look at this campus, built on the water!

00:06:24.500 --> 00:06:26.990
<b>Shibahama High School</b>

00:06:26.990 --> 00:06:28.740
The continued renovations, over time,

00:06:28.740 --> 00:06:30.490
have created a layout both
 complicated and inexplicable!

00:06:30.490 --> 00:06:32.490
A total lack of consistency 
between upper and lower levels!

00:06:32.490 --> 00:06:34.490
The bridges that go into town!

00:06:34.490 --> 00:06:36.410
<b>Shibahama High School</b>

00:06:34.490 --> 00:06:36.710
That clock, which isn't visible 
from most of the campus!

00:06:37.750 --> 00:06:39.800
Which means we usually end up looking at...

00:06:39.800 --> 00:06:42.020
The clock over on the coast!

00:06:42.020 --> 00:06:44.250
It's a public building shaped like a dungeon!

00:06:44.670 --> 00:06:47.220
I want to make an anime with 
this school as the setting!

00:06:47.220 --> 00:06:50.630
It's gonna look like this! What do you think?!

00:06:52.610 --> 00:06:56.140
You get fired up at the drop 
of a hat, don't you, Asakusa?

00:06:56.540 --> 00:06:58.260
I'm not sure what you want me to say...

00:07:01.650 --> 00:07:05.010
We just enrolled here, and you've
 got all this... stuff.

00:07:05.010 --> 00:07:09.540
Don't you have anything better 
to do with your energy?

00:07:09.540 --> 00:07:12.000
Come on, let's go to the anime 
club's screening, Kanamori!

00:07:13.210 --> 00:07:15.470
Make it four bottles of milk.

00:07:15.470 --> 00:07:16.870
You're taking advantage of me.

00:07:16.870 --> 00:07:19.180
<b>A/V Room A</b>

00:07:16.870 --> 00:07:19.870
<b>Anime Research Group
Special Screening</b>

00:07:19.870 --> 00:07:22.550
Go on, go on. Head in there.

00:07:23.050 --> 00:07:25.500
Please stop using me as a shield.

00:07:26.380 --> 00:07:28.150
Doesn't seem to be very busy...

00:07:28.150 --> 00:07:30.220
Let's sit in the back, Kanamori.

00:07:39.530 --> 00:07:40.830
Let's sit somewhere else!

00:07:40.830 --> 00:07:43.230
Start it up, please.

00:07:52.240 --> 00:07:54.240
<b>Conan
</b>of the Lost Island

00:07:55.100 --> 00:07:57.740
What about this is entertaining to you?

00:07:57.740 --> 00:08:00.090
You have this simple-looking, round machine,

00:08:00.090 --> 00:08:03.170
that can fly thanks to a 
unexplained anti-gravity device,

00:08:03.170 --> 00:08:05.710
which is depicted with an 
attention to fine details...

00:08:05.710 --> 00:08:07.580
Like how they pick it up with their hands!

00:08:07.580 --> 00:08:10.170
It's like when you push a car, 
hoping the engine will turn over!

00:08:10.170 --> 00:08:11.960
They're taking the obvious 
visual cues of the animation

00:08:11.960 --> 00:08:13.630
and using it to create an air of reality!

00:08:16.700 --> 00:08:18.470
The spacing of the frame...

00:08:18.470 --> 00:08:19.410
Establishing the location...

00:08:19.410 --> 00:08:21.460
The relaxed pace that's set by the running!

00:08:21.460 --> 00:08:24.480
The way it sets up the character's physicality!

00:08:25.020 --> 00:08:26.980
And this sense of scale!

00:08:26.980 --> 00:08:31.100
Look at the size contrast created 
in this crossover shot!

00:08:31.100 --> 00:08:32.490
And by having debris flying around,

00:08:32.490 --> 00:08:35.490
it creates a real sense of propulsion!

00:08:35.490 --> 00:08:38.010
And the movement of the air...

00:08:38.010 --> 00:08:40.200
With the character running against it,
 showing the resistance,

00:08:40.200 --> 00:08:41.330
and how it pushes them around...

00:08:41.330 --> 00:08:42.120
Right here!

00:08:42.120 --> 00:08:44.810
You take something that's totally implausible,
 but pass it off like it is!

00:08:44.810 --> 00:08:48.310
You take reality and then exaggerate 
it in a way that makes sense!

00:08:48.310 --> 00:08:51.760
A character moves around on top of 
a background, and it creates an entire world!

00:08:51.760 --> 00:08:55.330
Seeing a character wandering around a mysterious 
world fills you with a sense of adventure—

00:08:53.870 --> 00:08:56.170
I understand, and you can stop now.

00:08:56.170 --> 00:08:59.170
Getting more of an explanation than 
you asked for is excruciating.

00:08:59.170 --> 00:09:00.360
Sorry about that.

00:09:00.360 --> 00:09:03.560
I'll admit, anime is more 
complicated than I ever thought.

00:09:09.110 --> 00:09:10.620
Excuse me, you in the hat?

00:09:10.620 --> 00:09:14.400
Nice to meet you. I'm a first-year, too! 
Tsubame Mizusaki! I like anime, too!

00:09:14.400 --> 00:09:15.610
Wow, close! Uh, yes! Okay!

00:09:15.610 --> 00:09:18.010
Sorry to spring this on you,
but I need to borrow your hat!

00:09:18.010 --> 00:09:18.620
There she is.

00:09:18.620 --> 00:09:20.400
Whoa, are those MiBs?

00:09:20.400 --> 00:09:21.820
Thanks, see you later!

00:09:22.380 --> 00:09:24.620
Wait, my hat? Where'd it—

00:09:25.980 --> 00:09:27.470
<i>Conan!</i>

00:09:27.470 --> 00:09:29.030
<i>Kana!</i>

00:09:30.380 --> 00:09:32.370
A young girl, fleeing from villains...

00:09:32.370 --> 00:09:35.540
She's actually a famous fashion model...

00:09:35.540 --> 00:09:37.540
On top of being the daughter 
of some huge megacorp's boss.

00:09:37.540 --> 00:09:39.550
I thought there were anti-monopoly 
laws to get rid of those.

00:09:40.410 --> 00:09:42.680
This smells like cash...

00:09:42.680 --> 00:09:44.020
And adventure.

00:09:53.710 --> 00:09:55.940
<b>Strawberry Milk</b>

00:09:55.940 --> 00:09:56.970
<b>Strawberry Milk</b>

00:09:59.410 --> 00:10:00.330
There she is!

00:10:01.350 --> 00:10:02.550
Well, now...

00:10:07.750 --> 00:10:09.350
What are they talking about?

00:10:09.350 --> 00:10:10.620
I can't hear.

00:10:16.070 --> 00:10:18.760
If this is just a lecture, you didn't
 need to follow me to school.

00:10:19.170 --> 00:10:21.260
I was looking forward to the 
anime club's screening.

00:10:22.730 --> 00:10:27.020
I don't understand why I'm supposed to put
 on an act just because my parents both do it!

00:10:27.020 --> 00:10:30.520
I want a normal life! Going home with 
my friends, doing after school activities!

00:10:30.520 --> 00:10:34.270
Our orders are to keep you 
from joining the anime club.

00:10:35.230 --> 00:10:37.850
So if it was live action or any other 
kind of film club, it'd be fine?!

00:10:37.850 --> 00:10:38.240
Correct.

00:10:41.740 --> 00:10:43.170
Asakusa...

00:10:44.070 --> 00:10:47.250
Go and make friends with Mizusaki, all right?

00:10:50.750 --> 00:10:53.040
Being an animator is a real job!

00:10:53.040 --> 00:10:54.460
You breathe life into all kinds of roles!

00:10:54.460 --> 00:10:57.640
And not just people, but wind, 
the environment, machines...

00:10:57.640 --> 00:11:00.340
Sometimes they create performances 
bigger than anything live action could!

00:11:00.340 --> 00:11:01.370
Hey...

00:11:03.020 --> 00:11:05.010
You're the girl who had the hat...

00:11:05.010 --> 00:11:06.930
S-Sup! Sorry about the delay!

00:11:06.930 --> 00:11:08.600
I was late catching my bike! Can you believe it?

00:11:08.600 --> 00:11:09.980
Hey, it's almost 2!

00:11:09.980 --> 00:11:13.910
Why don't we chill on the roof and chow 
down our lunches, Tsubamecchy Mizusaki?

00:11:14.820 --> 00:11:17.630
Come on, there's a weirdo lurking around.

00:11:17.630 --> 00:11:18.950
Uh...

00:11:18.950 --> 00:11:21.240
Excuse me. Who are you, exactly?

00:11:22.270 --> 00:11:22.880
Run for it!

00:11:22.880 --> 00:11:24.370
Wait! Hey, hang on!

00:11:24.370 --> 00:11:24.990
Get back here!

00:11:25.510 --> 00:11:26.160
This way!

00:11:30.820 --> 00:11:32.040
Go up!

00:11:36.810 --> 00:11:37.670
There you are!

00:12:07.990 --> 00:12:10.250
That guy works for my parents!

00:12:10.250 --> 00:12:13.470
Thankfully, he's tough enough that
 that probably didn't hurt him.

00:12:13.470 --> 00:12:15.780
Man, you grabbed me when I was taking a sip,

00:12:15.780 --> 00:12:17.210
and now I'm covered in strawberry milk!

00:12:17.210 --> 00:12:18.910
I am so sorry.

00:12:18.910 --> 00:12:22.210
It's kind of crazy you thought he 
was some kind of bad guy, though.

00:12:22.210 --> 00:12:25.530
Sending someone to spy on you at school...

00:12:25.530 --> 00:12:27.680
Your parents keep you on 
a short leash, don't they?

00:12:27.680 --> 00:12:29.890
Whoa, Kanamori!

00:12:29.890 --> 00:12:32.220
They won't shut up about 
wanting me to be an actress.

00:12:32.220 --> 00:12:34.650
I'm not allowed to join the anime club,

00:12:34.650 --> 00:12:36.560
so I told him to get me a 
strawberry milk and slipped away.

00:12:38.820 --> 00:12:40.490
Not that it matters now.

00:12:40.490 --> 00:12:42.530
Wow, I smell like strawberry milk.

00:12:42.030 --> 00:12:44.460
That's Mizusaki Tsubame!

00:12:53.300 --> 00:12:56.460
No sense in chatting with an audience.
 Let's get you cleaned up.

00:12:58.990 --> 00:13:02.890
Kanamori, I'm not sure we should 
be butting in this much.

00:13:02.890 --> 00:13:07.180
What're you saying? First you save 
the princess, then comes the treasure.

00:13:07.180 --> 00:13:10.970
This isn't about rescuing a princess 
from a villain! It's a family disagreement!

00:13:10.970 --> 00:13:14.910
I know you heard her talk about anime, Asakusa.

00:13:15.270 --> 00:13:17.610
Let's just escort her to the laundromat for now.

00:13:17.610 --> 00:13:19.460
You're scheming something up,
aren't you, Kanamori?

00:13:22.470 --> 00:13:24.150
Is this where you sleep?

00:13:24.150 --> 00:13:26.620
Mizusaki, that's where actual people sleep!

00:13:26.620 --> 00:13:27.910
Wait, someone lives here?!

00:13:30.930 --> 00:13:32.010
Here we are.

00:13:32.010 --> 00:13:33.830
This is the laundromat?

00:13:33.830 --> 00:13:36.850
Admittedly, it doesn't exactly give
 off the impression of cleanliness.

00:13:36.850 --> 00:13:40.070
<b>Coin Laundry</b>

00:13:36.850 --> 00:13:40.070
<b>Rear Entrance
Ongyoku Bathhouse</b>

00:13:36.850 --> 00:13:40.070
Wow! Why is it in such an out-of-the-way place?

00:13:40.070 --> 00:13:43.590
There's a walkway on the second floor 
that leads to the Ongyoku Bathhouse!

00:13:43.590 --> 00:13:45.780
Why's the air conditioner on the door?

00:13:45.780 --> 00:13:47.490
Lots of places have cramped entrances.

00:13:50.770 --> 00:13:52.810
It's bigger on the inside than I expected.

00:13:52.810 --> 00:13:55.530
This place is a bit like my secret hideout.

00:13:52.810 --> 00:13:56.810
<b>Detergent</b>

00:13:53.310 --> 00:13:56.810
<b>Detergent</b>

00:13:56.810 --> 00:14:01.820
<b>Change Machine</b>

00:13:58.730 --> 00:14:00.020
Take this as an apology.

00:14:00.020 --> 00:14:01.820
Aw, you didn't have to...

00:14:08.270 --> 00:14:09.980
I've got some cash.

00:14:09.980 --> 00:14:11.070
Wow, thanks!

00:14:11.070 --> 00:14:13.520
Oh, no, just think of it as an investment.

00:14:13.520 --> 00:14:16.410
There's a waiting room on the second floor!

00:14:31.550 --> 00:14:34.080
<b>Coin Laundry</b>

00:14:42.910 --> 00:14:47.690
I love weird buildings like this. 
Can never draw them right, though...

00:14:49.500 --> 00:14:52.070
You draw, Mizusaki?

00:14:52.070 --> 00:14:54.380
Well, I want to be an animator.

00:14:54.380 --> 00:14:56.430
What kind of things do you draw?

00:14:59.300 --> 00:15:00.210
Take a look.

00:15:09.010 --> 00:15:11.110
What do you say, Asakusa?

00:15:11.650 --> 00:15:14.260
You can tell she's serious 
about being an animator.

00:15:14.260 --> 00:15:16.010
Lots of figure drawing,
 the kind I have trouble with.

00:15:16.010 --> 00:15:18.130
You draw too, Asakusa?!

00:15:18.130 --> 00:15:20.490
Uh, well, I...

00:15:21.650 --> 00:15:22.850
Here you go.

00:15:22.850 --> 00:15:24.010
Thanks!

00:15:24.010 --> 00:15:24.950
I'm gonna take a look.

00:15:26.480 --> 00:15:28.650
Damn it, Kanamori, who said you could—

00:15:30.970 --> 00:15:31.740
Let me go!

00:15:31.740 --> 00:15:35.240
These are... image boards 
and concept designs right?

00:15:36.650 --> 00:15:38.470
E-E-Exactly.

00:15:39.070 --> 00:15:41.000
What's an image board?

00:15:41.000 --> 00:15:43.900
It's the art done early in 
anime production to establish

00:15:43.900 --> 00:15:45.960
the look and feel of the world.

00:15:48.710 --> 00:15:49.800
Are you trying to kill me?!

00:15:49.800 --> 00:15:52.320
I've wanted to make anime 
ever since elementary school,

00:15:52.320 --> 00:15:54.250
and this is the kind of 
stuff I would always draw.

00:15:54.250 --> 00:15:57.930
But you're the first person to ever
 recognize that it was concept art.

00:15:58.860 --> 00:16:01.880
I've never met anyone who 
did concept design before.

00:16:01.880 --> 00:16:04.560
Most people just do character art. Including me.

00:16:05.390 --> 00:16:09.030
This is amazing... It's full of ideas.

00:16:14.380 --> 00:16:15.740
You want to try an overlay?

00:16:25.310 --> 00:16:26.850
It's like my art has a background!

00:16:26.850 --> 00:16:28.210
That worked better than I thought!

00:16:28.540 --> 00:16:29.980
Let's try with others.

00:16:29.980 --> 00:16:30.860
Yeah!

00:16:32.570 --> 00:16:33.740
How about this?

00:16:33.740 --> 00:16:34.670
Nice!

00:16:34.670 --> 00:16:35.450
And this?

00:16:35.450 --> 00:16:36.930
It looks good! This is fun!

00:16:38.250 --> 00:16:40.300
This is starting to get interesting!

00:16:40.850 --> 00:16:45.270
Mizusaki, how would you like to make 
anime with Midori Asakusa here?

00:16:46.140 --> 00:16:48.270
But I'm not allowed to join the anime club.

00:16:48.270 --> 00:16:50.700
That's right! Where'd that come from?!

00:16:50.700 --> 00:16:53.240
It's not like I have any experience, 
or know-how, or the guts to—

00:16:54.110 --> 00:16:56.180
Why should a pair of bright young people

00:16:56.180 --> 00:16:58.830
let nonsense like that stop them?

00:16:58.830 --> 00:17:02.340
Do you want to make anime or not?!

00:17:02.340 --> 00:17:03.620
If you can't join the anime club,

00:17:03.620 --> 00:17:06.370
then you can just start a new club of your own!

00:17:06.690 --> 00:17:09.750
We've got youth on our side.

00:17:09.750 --> 00:17:12.230
That means we don't stand to lose 
anything here. There's no risk involved.

00:17:12.230 --> 00:17:16.590
And I may not know anything about anime,
 but I can back you up in other ways.

00:17:16.590 --> 00:17:18.260
Why would you do that?

00:17:18.620 --> 00:17:23.140
Because a famous fashion model making 
anime sounds like a great way to rake in cash.

00:17:23.140 --> 00:17:24.250
You want money?!

00:17:27.650 --> 00:17:29.470
This ship is cool.

00:17:29.470 --> 00:17:33.390
You think? I just drew it because I 
felt like I needed to try and do something

00:17:33.390 --> 00:17:34.900
other than characters.

00:17:40.430 --> 00:17:43.290
Asakusa, try drawing some 
lines on the frame there!

00:17:43.290 --> 00:17:44.910
A couple of safety stripes, right?

00:17:49.110 --> 00:17:50.870
Go ahead and pull mine out!

00:17:56.420 --> 00:17:59.230
What do you suppose it does, though?

00:17:59.230 --> 00:18:02.030
I hadn't thought about it, 
but I guess it's for construction.

00:18:02.030 --> 00:18:04.470
In that case, some arms 
and winches would be good!

00:18:04.470 --> 00:18:05.260
Winches?

00:18:05.260 --> 00:18:06.840
Like the kind for spooling cables!

00:18:06.840 --> 00:18:08.270
Good idea! Put some on!

00:18:08.760 --> 00:18:10.030
Does it look good here?

00:18:10.030 --> 00:18:11.480
Wow!

00:18:12.030 --> 00:18:15.360
Y'know, I've never done any concept art before.

00:18:15.360 --> 00:18:17.430
I like setting up concepts.

00:18:17.430 --> 00:18:20.200
Did you ever draw a layout for a 
secret base when you were a kid?

00:18:20.510 --> 00:18:22.070
That was always a ton of fun!

00:18:23.330 --> 00:18:27.090
I remember adding traps
 and setting mines...

00:18:27.090 --> 00:18:29.250
Not sure who they were supposed to be for.

00:18:30.670 --> 00:18:33.270
The greatest world I can imagine!

00:18:33.270 --> 00:18:35.030
I draw to bring that world to life,

00:18:35.030 --> 00:18:39.410
so concepts are what it's all about!

00:18:41.750 --> 00:18:43.430
You're really something, Asakusa!

00:18:43.740 --> 00:18:47.380
In that case, let's keep going! 
Maybe it should have a light around here?

00:18:47.380 --> 00:18:49.940
That'd make the engine look kind of cramped.

00:18:49.940 --> 00:18:55.230
I'd like it better if it moved around 
in a more distinct way, though.

00:18:56.170 --> 00:18:58.450
How about something like this? 
Wings like you'd see on a bug.

00:18:58.450 --> 00:18:59.970
Oh, wow! That's awesome!

00:19:01.170 --> 00:19:03.530
It can't really land like that, though.

00:19:03.980 --> 00:19:05.870
Let's add some landing gear with 
tires for a counterweight,

00:19:05.870 --> 00:19:08.540
and turn the ducted fans into 
contra-rotating propellers.

00:19:08.540 --> 00:19:11.070
We can attach a tail to make 
it look like a dragonfly!

00:19:11.230 --> 00:19:20.240
<b>All-Purpose Manned Flying Pod
Kairi</b>

00:19:11.500 --> 00:19:12.290
It's done!

00:19:12.290 --> 00:19:13.140
Fantastic!

00:19:13.140 --> 00:19:16.790
And the wings' surfaces
are made of solar panels!

00:19:16.790 --> 00:19:17.900
Plus, the structure for

00:19:17.900 --> 00:19:20.240
the wing joints is modeled after 
real exoskeletons and muscle fibers!

00:19:20.950 --> 00:19:21.890
It's tiny!

00:19:21.890 --> 00:19:23.600
It has to be, to be light enough.

00:19:29.350 --> 00:19:32.350
All right, let's do a motion 
check for the wings.

00:19:38.870 --> 00:19:40.010
All good!

00:19:45.280 --> 00:19:46.780
Hold it!

00:19:47.660 --> 00:19:49.470
Oh, no! Let's get out of here!

00:19:50.550 --> 00:19:52.480
The switch for the launch 
catapult is on the outside.

00:19:52.480 --> 00:19:53.250
I'll go!

00:19:55.610 --> 00:19:57.000
There was a door here?

00:19:59.190 --> 00:20:00.110
Is this it?

00:20:05.140 --> 00:20:05.620
Huh?

00:20:05.620 --> 00:20:07.330
<i>It says number three is empty!</i>

00:20:07.330 --> 00:20:10.020
That means there's no steam pressure! 
The catapult's not gonna work!

00:20:10.020 --> 00:20:12.440
I'll push! Kanamori, help me!

00:20:12.440 --> 00:20:13.980
Whatever...

00:20:20.730 --> 00:20:23.210
Move!

00:20:35.470 --> 00:20:39.650
All right! Get in, you two!

00:20:52.270 --> 00:20:54.810
Come on!

00:21:09.280 --> 00:21:11.860
It worked! We're actually flying!

00:21:14.230 --> 00:21:15.920
<b>Ice</b>

00:21:28.180 --> 00:21:29.850
Is there no way out of here?!

00:21:29.850 --> 00:21:31.860
There are massive skyscrapers 
in every direction!

00:21:31.860 --> 00:21:33.350
This is bad.

00:21:33.350 --> 00:21:34.350
Over there!

00:21:34.350 --> 00:21:35.150
It's too narrow!

00:21:35.150 --> 00:21:35.850
We'll fly sideways!

00:21:35.850 --> 00:21:37.260
It's not gonna work!

00:21:38.620 --> 00:21:39.360
Huh?

00:21:39.360 --> 00:21:40.580
What? What is it?

00:21:40.580 --> 00:21:42.060
One of the wings isn't responding!

00:21:42.650 --> 00:21:44.320
It took a hit!

00:21:44.320 --> 00:21:46.320
We're gonna crash!

00:21:46.320 --> 00:21:48.300
The three of us can figure this out!

00:21:48.300 --> 00:21:49.900
Kanamori, let's try and shift the weight!

00:21:49.900 --> 00:21:51.200
Oh, for the love of...

00:21:58.210 --> 00:22:00.250
Yeah!

00:22:10.750 --> 00:22:12.150
Ow, ow, ow...

00:22:18.340 --> 00:22:23.150
This... It's the greatest world.

00:22:36.530 --> 00:22:39.480
Is it just me, or did we go somewhere awesome?

00:22:39.480 --> 00:22:41.940
It felt like we saw something amazing.

00:22:42.550 --> 00:22:44.630
Oh, shoot, I need to go!

00:22:44.630 --> 00:22:46.760
The new anime by the animation dream team of

00:22:46.760 --> 00:22:48.820
Inoue-san, Ohira-san, and Iso-san is gonna air!

00:22:48.820 --> 00:22:49.360
Can't you record it?

00:22:49.360 --> 00:22:50.650
I've gotta see it live!

00:22:52.940 --> 00:22:53.990
Which way is the station?!

00:22:53.990 --> 00:22:55.640
I'll show you the shortest route!

00:22:55.640 --> 00:22:57.930
I am not running.

00:22:57.930 --> 00:22:59.910
But you always get better times than me.

00:22:59.910 --> 00:23:01.800
Mizusaki, how fast can you do 100 meters?

00:23:01.800 --> 00:23:03.950
When I was little, I used to say 
I could do it in one second.

00:23:03.950 --> 00:23:05.650
Then we can get to the station in eight seconds!

00:23:05.650 --> 00:23:09.490
Whoever's last to the station 
has to treat me to something.

00:23:09.490 --> 00:23:10.480
See ya!

00:23:10.480 --> 00:23:11.540
Hey, wait!

00:23:11.540 --> 00:23:12.320
That's cheating!

00:23:12.320 --> 00:23:14.690
You two are the ones who 
decided to just stand around!

00:23:14.690 --> 00:23:15.460
Why wouldn't we?!

00:23:15.460 --> 00:23:17.230
Kanamori, you're too fast!

00:23:19.970 --> 00:23:24.450
<i>Your washing is done. Please unload the machine.</i>

00:23:24.450 --> 00:23:28.350
<i>Your washing is done. Please unload the machine.</i>

00:24:55.970 --> 00:25:00.250
<b>Illustration by Aoki Toshinao</b>
